From: ohayoyogi <77435669+ohayoyogi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:19:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkisp1: allocate at least four capture buffers

Since min_queued_buffers went from 3 to 1, VIDIOC_REQBUFS no longer
rounds a small request up to four buffers. GStreamer's v4l2src asks for
two when the downstream allocation query carries no minimum (for example
behind "identity drop-allocation=true"). With two buffers, one is in
userspace being copied while the other is being filled, so the main path
writes into the dummy buffer for the frames in between: a TC358743 at
720p60 delivered 40 fps through v4l2src on 6.18, 60 fps on 6.12.

Keep min_queued_buffers at 1, so streaming still starts with a single
buffer, and set min_reqbufs_allocation to 4.
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c
index bff68d02d..47b96eb7c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c
@@ -1620,6 +1620,14 @@ static int rkisp1_register_capture(struct rkisp1_capture *cap)
 	q->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
 	q->buf_struct_size = sizeof(struct rkisp1_buffer);
 	q->min_queued_buffers = 1;
+	/*
+	 * Applications that ask for the minimum (GStreamer v4l2src takes two
+	 * when nothing downstream asks for more) leave the hardware writing
+	 * into the dummy buffer while they hold the other one, and every few
+	 * frames are lost. Allocate four, as before min_queued_buffers came
+	 * down from three.
+	 */
+	q->min_reqbufs_allocation = 4;
 	q->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC;
 	q->lock = &node->vlock;
 	q->dev = cap->rkisp1->dev;
-- 
2.43.0

